values ('d809b07f-e0a6-5872-8ee0-dbdba5f9beb3', 'rg5-word-parts-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Meeting the Author$q$, $q$Amara had read every book in the Harbor Fox series twice. So when the author, Mr. Delgado, came to the town library, she arrived an hour early.

The room was already filling up. By the time Mr. Delgado walked in, the audience had grown to more than a hundred people. Everyone grew quiet so they could hear him.

Mr. Delgado read a chapter from his newest book. A baby in the back started to cry, and he had to interrupt his reading for a moment. He smiled and waited, then picked up right where he had stopped.

During the question time, a boy said the fox in the books could never swim across the bay. Mr. Delgado did not contradict him. Instead, he said, "Good point. Maybe that is why the fox always takes the ferry."

Afterward, Amara stood in a long line to get his autograph. When she reached the table, he signed his name inside her book in curly blue ink. To Amara, he was more famous than any movie star.$q$, 'draft')
