-- Passage rg5-word-parts-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('dd8926fb-a5c6-5679-946e-60f15046f137', 'rg5-word-parts-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Trains Under the City$q$, $q$In many large cities, thousands of people ride trains that travel underground. These trains run through a subway, a system of tunnels below the streets.

Cities built subways because the streets above were crowded. Wagons, carts, and people filled every road. Building tunnels gave the city a new way to transport people without adding more traffic on top.

Digging a subway is hard work. Workers must avoid water pipes, power lines, and the foundations of tall buildings. At each busy intersection, crews had to dig carefully, because two streets crossed right above them.

Today, a supervisor watches over each part of the system. From a control room, the supervisor can see where every train is. If a train stops, the supervisor tells the others to slow down.

Some subways never close. Trains rumble along the tracks even after midnight, carrying nurses, bakers, and others who work late hours. For these riders, the subway is the most dependable form of transportation in the city.$q$, 'draft')
