insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('44cba718-9331-5bff-a0fd-c5d68640ef37', 'rg5-word-parts-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Kite Festival$q$, $q$Every April, the town of Bellridge holds a kite festival in Riverside Park. Kite fliers come from many places, and the sky fills with color.

This year, Rafael and his aunt brought a dragon kite they had made together. It was long and red, with a tail that rippled in the wind. Their kite was flexible, so it bent in strong gusts instead of snapping.

The main attraction was a giant whale kite as big as a school bus. People crowded around to watch as six helpers lifted it into the air. A park worker supervised the launch and kept everyone at a safe distance. Rafael stared up at it with his mouth open.

Rafael's aunt brought a portable stand to hold the kite spool. It folded up small enough to fit in her backpack, and she set it up in seconds.

In the afternoon, the wind suddenly died. Dozens of kites drifted down, but Rafael's dragon hung in midair a moment longer before it floated to the grass. A judge walked over and said that the dragon had the best design of the day. Rafael could hardly believe it.$q$, 'draft')
