   $q$The author writes that "the game belongs to all of them, not only the stars." What belief does this sentence reveal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Star players should be kept off the field so others can score goals.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"exaggerates-position"},{"text":"For young children, including every player matters more than winning.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Every child in the league will become a star once they turn nine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Children under eight cannot tell who is the best player on a team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$For young children, including every player matters more than winning.$q$, $q$The sentence sums up the author's view that shared playing time is what young players need most. The author never says strong players should be benched, only that everyone now plays the same amount.$q$, 'draft', '3ca7b49f-54a3-590a-9801-d96b1798b506')
