insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('324e929e-0e5b-537e-82cc-0f7d3bf9a13b', 'rg6-comparing-texts-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Holding the String$q$, $q$Text 1: Kite Day (a story)

Mateo had built his kite from tissue paper and two thin sticks. At the park, he ran as fast as he could, and the kite bounced along the grass behind him. Each time it lifted, he yanked the string to pull it higher. Each time, it dove back to the ground.

His older cousin Priya watched from a bench. "You keep holding it too tight," she said. "Give it some line and wait for the wind."

Mateo frowned, but he tried again. This time he stood still. When a gust came, he let the string slide slowly through his fingers. The kite wobbled, then climbed. It rose past the treetops until it was a small red dot against the clouds.

"I barely did anything," Mateo said.

Priya smiled. "That was the hard part."

Text 2: The Line (a poem)

I wanted to steer it,
to tug it up high.
I pulled and I pulled,
and it fell from the sky.

So I loosened my grip.
I let the line go.
The wind did the lifting.
I just had to know

that the harder I held,
the lower it flew.
Some things only rise
when you trust them to.$q$, 'draft')
