insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('cbfb5a7c-1d03-5e4e-89c9-c1bae58e1269', 'rg6-comparing-texts-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Pieces of Home$q$, $q$Text 1: The Quilt Table (a story)

When Leilani's grandmother moved in, she brought a sewing machine and a big box of old clothes. "These are too small or too worn to wear," Grandma Keala said. "But they are not too small to keep."

They spread the clothes across the kitchen table. Grandma cut a square from a yellow sundress. "Your mother wore this to her first day of school," she said. She cut another from a faded flannel shirt. "Your grandfather wore this when he fixed the fence every spring."

Leilani found her own baby blanket, soft and green with tiny stars. She hesitated. Then she handed it over.

For three weeks, they sewed in the evenings. Leilani learned to pin the corners so they lined up. When the quilt was finished, she spread it over her bed and traced the squares with her finger. She knew a story for every one.

Text 2: Patchwork (a poem)

Here is the blue of my brother's jeans,
the ones with the knees worn through.
Here is the red of my mother's scarf
she wore when the snow was new.

Here is a stripe from a summer shirt,
a square from a holiday dress.
Each piece was something we wore and loved.
Now it is something we bless.

At night when I pull the corners up,
I am wrapped in the people I know.
The threads hold more than cloth together.
They hold the years we let go.$q$, 'draft')
