-- Passage rg6-comparing-texts-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('283a7be9-f4eb-57f6-acbd-625161abbe07', 'rg6-comparing-texts-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$After the Snow$q$, $q$Text 1: Before Sunrise (a story)

The storm dropped fourteen inches of snow on Cedar Street overnight. At six in the morning, Hana's father knocked on her door. "Get your boots," he whispered. "We have a job to do."

Across the street lived Mrs. Lindqvist, who walked with a cane. Her front walk had disappeared under a smooth white blanket. Hana and her father shoveled it quietly, one scrape at a time, while the street was still dark. They cleared her steps and sprinkled salt on the bottom one. Then they went home without knocking.

At breakfast, Hana watched through the window. Mrs. Lindqvist opened her door, looked down at the clean path, and stood still for a long moment. Then she smiled and waved at no one in particular.

"Should we tell her it was us?" Hana asked.

Her father shook his head. "Look at her face," he said. "That is the whole reward."

Text 2: Snow Day on Birch Lane (a poem)

By nine the street is full of shovels,
scraping out a song.
The Patels dig the Garcias out.
The twins hand mittens along.

Old Mr. Abara brings a thermos.
Ms. Chen brings extra salt.
When one car spins its tires in place,
five neighbors call out, halt!

Then everyone together pushes.
The car rolls free at last.
We cheer as loud as any crowd
at any game we've passed.

The snow fell on each house alone.
We shovel it as one.
By noon the whole lane sparkles clear
beneath a winter sun.$q$, 'draft')
