-- Passage rg6-comparing-texts-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('56bd0145-1b4b-5dbe-936a-5ef7bed48e5b', 'rg6-comparing-texts-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Together Is Faster$q$, $q$Text 1: The Handoff (a story)

Sofia was the fastest runner on the Riverside relay team, and everyone knew it. At practice, she complained about the handoffs. "If I could just run all four laps myself, we would win," she said.

Coach Imani handed her a stopwatch. "Time it," she said. Sofia ran four laps alone. Then the team ran four laps, passing the baton smoothly from Kwame to Rosa to Eli to Sofia. The team's time was nineteen seconds faster.

"Fresh legs on every lap," the coach said. "Nobody wins a relay alone."

After that, Sofia stayed late to practice the handoff with Eli. She learned to start running before he reached her, with her hand stretched back. At the city meet, the baton slid into her palm without a pause. Riverside won by a step, and Sofia hugged all three of her teammates at the finish line.

Text 2: Eight Oars (a poem)

Eight of us sit in a narrow boat.
Eight of us lean and reach.
If one pulls early, the boat will rock.
If one pulls late, the same.

No one is the strongest here.
No one is the star.
The water only listens
when we move as one oar.

Catch, and drive, and finish, and float.
We breathe the same slow breath.
The river carries all of us
because we carry it together.$q$, 'draft')
