   $q$In paragraph 5, water in Rome became "abundant." What does "abundant" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"very hard to find","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"clean and safe to drink","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"available in large amounts","is_correct":true},{"text":"costly for ordinary people","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$available in large amounts$q$, $q$The next sentence says "There was plenty" for fountains, baths, and gardens, so abundant means available in large amounts. Clean water is mentioned in paragraph 1, but this paragraph is about how much water there was.$q$, 'draft', 'a98ba625-18e8-5214-9b7f-88deae86109f')
