   $q$In paragraph 4, Nana is "meticulous" about cutting the squares. What does "meticulous" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"quick and careless with the work","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"very careful about every detail","is_correct":true},{"text":"unsure of how to begin a project","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"bossy and unkind to other people","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$very careful about every detail$q$, $q$She "measured every square twice," lined up her ruler "with care," and fixed even slightly crooked squares, all signs of great care. Asking Zara to redo squares shows high standards, not unkindness, and Nana laughs warmly later in the story.$q$, 'draft', '6487fd3f-6c47-50ed-91c0-c2f89aff8975')
