   $q$Which detail best supports the inference that water clocks were valued for fairness, not just for telling the hour?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Water dripped out of a tiny hole near the bottom at a steady rate.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Some were used to time speeches so each speaker received a fair turn.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Lines on the inside showed how much time had passed as water fell.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"They could be used at night, when sundials were of no help at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Some were used to time speeches so each speaker received a fair turn.$q$, $q$Timing speeches so each speaker got "a fair turn" shows the clocks were used to treat people equally. Working at night is a real advantage, but it is about telling time, not fairness.$q$, 'draft', '93912662-8468-5a0e-8e1f-819ac3868486')
