   $q$In paragraph 2, the author writes that "the wind was restless." What does this personification tell the reader about the wind?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It was too cold for the people who came to the festival.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It was worried about the kite contest, just like Tomasz.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It was tired and could barely lift the kites off the ground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It kept moving and pushing things around instead of staying calm.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It kept moving and pushing things around instead of staying calm.$q$, $q$A restless person cannot sit still, and the next sentence shows the wind tugging jackets, rattling poles, and chasing cups. Wind cannot actually feel worried; the word describes its constant motion.$q$, 'draft', '781cc872-cb16-529e-bd69-22390ad00008')
