   $q$In paragraph 5, Lucia's seams "wandered across the cloth like a lost puppy." What does this simile tell the reader?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A puppy walked across the fabric while she was sewing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She lost the cloth and had to search the house for it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Her stitches were perfectly straight from the very start.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Her stitches were crooked and went in different directions.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her stitches were crooked and went in different directions.$q$, $q$A lost puppy wanders here and there without a clear path, so the seams were crooked. Later the passage says that by late afternoon "the seams were straight," showing they were not straight at first.$q$, 'draft', '338e4de6-03eb-59ed-98b0-cf3e3bb871b0')
