   $q$In paragraph 2, the pigeon "would shoot toward home like an arrow." What does this simile show about the pigeon's flight?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It was hunted by people carrying bows.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It flew fast and straight toward its home.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It flew in circles before landing on a ship.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It flew slowly and stopped often to rest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It flew fast and straight toward its home.$q$, $q$An arrow travels quickly in a straight line, so the simile shows a fast, direct flight home. The passage says pigeons were "fast," which rules out a slow flight.$q$, 'draft', '1f1ed3c4-411a-5394-b541-ca3671e3ad70')
