-- Passage rg6-figurative-language-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('8c671e9a-bac7-5fc2-8a86-4b9c1076c51a', 'rg6-figurative-language-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-figurative-language'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Patient Player$q$, $q$Darnell Brooks had played chess in the library club for two years, but he had never entered a real tournament. On Saturday morning, the school gym was filled with long tables and ticking clocks. The room was so quiet that Darnell could hear his own breathing.

His first opponent was a girl named Mei Lin, who looked calm and confident. She moved her pieces quickly, almost carelessly. Darnell studied the board for a long time before each move. His friend Javier had called him slow, but Darnell preferred to think of himself as patient.

Halfway through the game, Mei Lin's knight slipped behind Darnell's defenses like a fox entering a henhouse. Darnell's queen was trapped. His heart sank to his shoes. He took a deep breath and reminded himself that a game is not over until the king falls.

He looked for a way out. Slowly, an idea began to bloom. If he gave up his queen, he could open a path for his rook. It was a risky plan, but it was his only chance.

Mei Lin took the queen with a satisfied nod. Three moves later, her face fell. Darnell's rook marched down the open line, and her king had nowhere to hide.

After the game, Mei Lin shook his hand. "That was sneaky," she said, then laughed. "I mean clever." Darnell smiled all the way home.$q$, 'draft')
