   $q$In paragraph 3, "His heart sank to his shoes." What does this phrase show about Darnell?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He felt excited because he was about to win the game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"He suddenly felt very discouraged when his queen was trapped.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He bent down to tie his shoes during the chess match.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"He felt sleepy because the room was so quiet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-emotion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He suddenly felt very discouraged when his queen was trapped.$q$, $q$The phrase comes right after "Darnell's queen was trapped," so it shows a sudden, heavy feeling of disappointment. He was not about to win at that moment; he was in trouble.$q$, 'draft', '8c671e9a-bac7-5fc2-8a86-4b9c1076c51a')
