   $q$In paragraph 2, Javier called Darnell "slow," but Darnell thought of himself as "patient." Why does Darnell prefer the word "patient"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Patient\" means he is sick and needs to visit the school nurse during the game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-word-sense"},{"text":"\"Patient\" means the opposite of \"slow,\" so it shows he actually plays very fast.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-denotation"},{"text":"\"Patient\" has a positive feeling, suggesting he takes time on purpose to think well.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Patient\" has a negative feeling, suggesting he is lazy and does not try hard.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Patient" has a positive feeling, suggesting he takes time on purpose to think well.$q$, $q$Both words describe taking a long time, but "slow" sounds like a weakness while "patient" sounds like a strength. Darnell still studies the board "for a long time," so he does not play fast.$q$, 'draft', '8c671e9a-bac7-5fc2-8a86-4b9c1076c51a')
