   $q$In paragraph 4, "Slowly, an idea began to bloom." What does the word "bloom" suggest about Darnell's idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It came from a flower that was sitting on the chess table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It was a plan that Javier had given him before the game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It grew gradually in his mind until it became a full plan.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It disappeared as soon as he started to think about it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It grew gradually in his mind until it became a full plan.$q$, $q$A flower blooms slowly, opening a little at a time, and the sentence begins with "Slowly." The idea grew into a plan to give up his queen, so it did not disappear.$q$, 'draft', '8c671e9a-bac7-5fc2-8a86-4b9c1076c51a')
