   $q$In paragraph 2, owl eyes "gather every scrap of light, the way a bucket collects raindrops." What does this comparison show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Owl eyes fill with water whenever it rains at night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Owl eyes can move in every direction like a swinging bucket.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Owl eyes take in as much of the dim light as they possibly can.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Owl eyes block out light so the owl can sleep in the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Owl eyes take in as much of the dim light as they possibly can.$q$, $q$A bucket catches every drop that falls into it, just as huge owl eyes catch even small amounts of light in the dark. The text says owls "cannot move their eyes," so the comparison is not about movement.$q$, 'draft', '21993381-eb45-59f2-a452-331fee5c2025')
