   $q$In paragraph 4, the owl's feathers "muffle the noise." Which word means the OPPOSITE of "muffle"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"amplify","is_correct":true},{"text":"flutter","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"hush","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"synonym-not-antonym"},{"text":"soften","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"synonym-not-antonym"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$amplify$q$, $q$To muffle a sound is to make it quieter, so the opposite is "amplify," which means to make it louder. "Soften" and "hush" are synonyms of muffle, not opposites.$q$, 'draft', '21993381-eb45-59f2-a452-331fee5c2025')
