  ('9faa1932-7499-524b-a6a6-5b031afe557e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 5, the author calls an owl "a quiet partner, guarding the fields while everyone sleeps." What does this metaphor suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Owls help farmers by eating rodents at night, even though no one sees them working.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Owls are trained by farmers to stand watch and warn them about strangers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Owls stay awake all day so that farmers can take a rest in the afternoon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Owls harm the fields at night by eating the crops while farmers are asleep.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Owls help farmers by eating rodents at night, even though no one sees them working.$q$, $q$The paragraph says owls "eat many mice and other rodents," so they protect the fields like a helpful partner during the night. Owls eat rodents, not crops, so they do not harm the fields.$q$, 'draft', '21993381-eb45-59f2-a452-331fee5c2025')
