-- Passage rg6-figurative-language-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('e5080a56-dc71-566b-8a44-20c28281b114', 'rg6-figurative-language-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-figurative-language'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Night the Lights Went Out$q$, $q$The storm arrived on Tuesday afternoon, and by dinnertime the snow was knee deep. Then, with a soft click, the lights went out. The refrigerator stopped humming. The house fell silent, as if it were holding its breath.

Priya's little brother, Arjun, grabbed her sleeve. "It's so dark," he said. Priya found the flashlight in the kitchen drawer and switched it on. A circle of yellow light wobbled across the ceiling.

Their father lit candles and set them on the table. The small flames bobbed and swayed, painting the walls with gold.

Without the television or computers, the family did not know what to do at first. Then Mom pulled an old board game from the closet. The box was battered, and two pieces were missing, so they used buttons instead.

Soon the kitchen was bursting with laughter. Arjun won the first round and strutted around the table like a proud rooster. Priya pretended to be annoyed, but she was having more fun than she had had in weeks.

The power came back at ten o'clock. The lights blinked on, and the refrigerator grumbled back to life. Arjun groaned. "Can we turn them off again?" he asked.

Priya laughed. She realized the storm had not stolen their evening at all. It had handed them a gift.$q$, 'draft')
