   $q$In paragraph 6, "the refrigerator grumbled back to life." Why does the author use "grumbled" instead of a word like "sang"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Grumbled\" suggests a low, rumbling, slightly complaining sound, which fits a refrigerator starting up.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Grumbled\" shows that Arjun was the one complaining loudly while standing next to the refrigerator.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-subject"},{"text":"\"Grumbled\" shows that the refrigerator was broken and would not work after the storm ended.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"\"Grumbled\" suggests a cheerful, musical sound, which shows the family was glad the power was back.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Grumbled" suggests a low, rumbling, slightly complaining sound, which fits a refrigerator starting up.$q$, $q$To grumble is to complain in a low voice, so the word fits the deep hum of a refrigerator restarting. "Sang" would suggest a happy, musical sound, and the refrigerator did come "back to life," so it was not broken.$q$, 'draft', 'e5080a56-dc71-566b-8a44-20c28281b114')
