  ('e8765f36-8289-56d6-8bad-308dab69247b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 7, Priya realizes "the storm had not stolen their evening at all. It had handed them a gift." What does this mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The family received a present from a neighbor after the power came back on.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"The storm ruined the evening, and Priya was glad when the lights returned.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The power outage, which seemed like a problem, actually gave the family a fun evening together.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Someone broke into the house during the storm and took the family's games.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The power outage, which seemed like a problem, actually gave the family a fun evening together.$q$, $q$The family laughed over a board game, and Priya had "more fun than she had had in weeks," so the outage gave them something good. Arjun even wants the lights off again, so the evening was not ruined.$q$, 'draft', 'e5080a56-dc71-566b-8a44-20c28281b114')
