   $q$Why does writing the passage as the narrator's own journal suit this story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It hides the narrator's feelings so the reader must guess them alone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It lets the reader hear what every student in the program was thinking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-first-and-third-person"},{"text":"It allows Dr. Varga to explain the science in Dr. Varga's own words and voice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-narrator-with-character"},{"text":"It shows the narrator's private feelings changing from one day to the next.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows the narrator's private feelings changing from one day to the next.$q$, $q$Journal entries let the narrator share thoughts such as "this week was a mistake" and "Now I wonder," so readers can trace the narrator's change across the week. A journal shows only the narrator's thoughts, not every student's.$q$, 'draft', '1f5588e8-69e4-578e-b90f-fc8de6e7fac0')
